IMPORT prelude

-- National Heritage Board Act 1993 (Singapore) -- what the Act decides for a person outside the Board: entry on private land for
-- archaeological investigation and what may be taken (s 46), the offence of copying the Board's symbol (s 47), the secrecy duty of
-- members, staff and agents (s 47A), the Board's immunity (s 48), pre-1993 gifts meant for the National Museum (s 14), when the Board
-- may dispose of objects in its collections (s 15(3)-(5)) and lend against a donor's condition (s 16(3)), and three rules of the
-- Schedule a member meets (disqualification, para 9; vacation of office, para 7; quorum and casting vote, para 11), with the Board's
-- size (s 5(1)) and the sealing of documents (s 4(2)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/NHBA1993.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates all
-- amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the latest amendment annotated in the
-- body is Act 36 of 2021 (ss 31(1), 46(10)). The retrieval record (NHBA1993.meta.json) calls it the current version as at
-- 3 October 2026.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0190 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper question yet.
-- Not encoded: the Board's functions and powers (ss 6, 7), committees and delegation (s 8), ministerial directions (s 10), museums
-- and directors (ss 11, 12), the 1993 vesting of the National Museum's objects (s 13), the Minister's transfers (s 15(2)), staff
-- (ss 28, 29), funds, borrowing, shares, grants, tax status and the Endowment Fund (ss 31-36; see NOTES.md on s 34), the 1993
-- transfer of assets and employees (ss 37-45), regulations (s 49), transitional provisions (s 50), and the rest of the Schedule.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `National Heritage Board Act 1993 -- heritage`

§§ `46 -- entry on land for archaeological investigation`

-- s 46(1): a person "specifically authorised in writing by the Board, after giving not less than 24 hours' notice in writing to the
-- occupier ... and on production of his or her authority, if so required by or on behalf of the occupier, may enter ... at all
-- reasonable times upon any land which the Board has reason to believe contains any ancient monument and may make excavations".
-- (2): no entry to "any dwelling house or any building, park, garden, pleasure ground or other land used for the amenity or
-- convenience of a dwelling house except with the occupier's consent".
-- (3): no excavation "except with the consent of every person whose consent ... would, apart from that subsection, be required".
GIVEN `authorised in writing by the Board` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `hours of written notice to the occupier` IS A NUMBER,
      `the occupier asked to see the authority` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the authority was produced` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `at a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Board has reason to believe the land holds an ancient monument` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a dwelling house or land used for its amenity` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the occupier consented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the entry is authorised by section 46` IF
        `authorised in writing by the Board`
    AND `hours of written notice to the occupier` AT LEAST 24
    AND ((NOT `the occupier asked to see the authority`) OR `the authority was produced`)
    AND `at a reasonable time`
    AND `the Board has reason to believe the land holds an ancient monument`
    AND ((NOT `a dwelling house or land used for its amenity`) OR `the occupier consented`)

GIVEN `the entry is lawful` IS A BOOLEAN, `every consent otherwise required was given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an excavation may be made` IF
    `the entry is lawful` AND `every consent otherwise required was given`

-- s 46(6): the entrant "may take temporary custody of any object of archaeological or historical interest discovered" and remove it.
-- (7): the Board "may not retain the object without the owner's consent beyond the period that may be reasonably required" for
-- examining, recording, testing or treatment. (8): nothing affects the Government's rights in treasure trove (not encoded).
GIVEN `still within the period reasonably required` IS A BOOLEAN, `the owner consented to longer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may keep the object` IF
    `still within the period reasonably required` OR `the owner consented to longer`

-- s 46(9): "Any person who wilfully obstructs or hinders any person in the exercise of the powers conferred by this section shall be
-- guilty of an offence" -- fine up to $5,000, imprisonment up to one year, or both.
-- INFERENCE: obstructing an entry the section does not authorise (no notice, a home without consent) is not "the exercise of the
-- powers conferred by this section", so it is not this offence.
GIVEN `wilfully obstructed or hindered` IS A BOOLEAN, `the power was being exercised as section 46 allows` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `obstruction is an offence under section 46` IF
    `wilfully obstructed or hindered` AND `the power was being exercised as section 46 allows`

§§ `47, 47A -- the Board's symbol and secrecy`

-- s 47(2): "A person who, without the permission of the Board, uses a symbol or representation identical with that of the Board or
-- which so resembles the Board's symbol or representation as to deceive or cause confusion, or to be likely to deceive or cause
-- confusion, shall be guilty of an offence" -- fine up to $5,000, imprisonment up to one year, or both.
GIVEN `uses a symbol or representation` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `identical with the Board's` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `resembles it so as to be likely to deceive or confuse` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `has the Board's permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `using the symbol is an offence` IF
        `uses a symbol or representation`
    AND (`identical with the Board's` OR `resembles it so as to be likely to deceive or confuse`)
    AND (NOT `has the Board's permission`)

-- s 47A(1): no person who "is or has been" a member, officer, employee or agent of the Board, or a member of a committee it appointed,
-- may disclose information "relating to the affairs of the Board or of any other person" obtained in the performance of functions,
-- "Except for the purpose of the performance of his or her functions or the discharge of his or her duties or when lawfully required
-- to do so by any court or where required or allowed by the provisions of this Act or any written law".
-- (2): fine up to $2,000, imprisonment up to 12 months, or both.
GIVEN `is or was a member, officer, employee, agent or committee member` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the information came to them through their duties` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `disclosed it` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `for the performance of their functions` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `lawfully required by a court` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `required or allowed by written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure is an offence` IF
        `is or was a member, officer, employee, agent or committee member`
    AND `the information came to them through their duties`
    AND `disclosed it`
    AND (NOT `for the performance of their functions`)
    AND (NOT `lawfully required by a court`)
    AND (NOT `required or allowed by written law`)

DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `obstructing archaeological entry`
    `using the Board's symbol`
    `breaching secrecy`

-- Maximum fine in dollars, and maximum imprisonment in months, from ss 46(9), 47(2) and 47A(2).
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `obstructing archaeological entry` THEN 5000
    WHEN `using the Board's symbol` THEN 5000
    WHEN `breaching secrecy` THEN 2000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `obstructing archaeological entry` THEN 12
    WHEN `using the Board's symbol` THEN 12
    WHEN `breaching secrecy` THEN 12

§§ `48 -- immunity`

-- s 48: "No suit or other legal proceedings shall lie against the Board, any member, officer or employee of the Board or other person
-- acting under the direction of the Board for anything which is in good faith done or intended to be done in the execution or
-- purported execution of this Act or the Preservation of Monuments Act 2009."
GIVEN `done in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `in the execution or purported execution of this Act or the 2009 Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a suit may lie against the Board or its people` IF
    NOT (`done in good faith` AND `in the execution or purported execution of this Act or the 2009 Act`)

§§ `14 -- gifts made before 1 August 1993 that take effect later`

-- s 14(1): a gift "(by will or otherwise)" contained in an instrument "made or executed before 1 August 1993 but coming into effect on
-- or after that date" which "would, apart from this Act, have vested an interest in property ... in the Government for the purposes
-- of the National Museum". (2): it vests in the Board instead "in the absence of any contrary intention expressed in that or another
-- instrument made by the testator or donor". Dates are written YYYYMMDD.
GIVEN `instrument made on` IS A NUMBER,
      `gift takes effect on` IS A NUMBER,
      `would have vested in the Government for the National Museum` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the donor expressed a contrary intention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the gift vests in the Board` IF
        `instrument made on` LESS THAN 19930801
    AND `gift takes effect on` AT LEAST 19930801
    AND `would have vested in the Government for the National Museum`
    AND (NOT `the donor expressed a contrary intention`)

§§ `15, 16 -- disposing of and lending collection objects`

DECLARE `Means of disposal` IS ONE OF sale, exchange, gift, destruction

-- s 15(3): the Board "may not dispose of an object of significant national or historical value" in its collections unless it is
-- "(a) a duplicate ... or (b) in the Board's opinion unsuitable for retention", "and the disposal is done with the prior approval of
-- the Minister and by way of sale, exchange or gift".
-- (4): it may dispose "(by whatever means, including destruction)" of an object "useless for the purposes of its collections by reason
-- of damage, physical deterioration or infestation by destructive organisms"; (5) "despite a trust or condition (express or implied)
-- prohibiting or restricting the disposal". (6): the money must go to acquiring objects (not encoded).
-- INFERENCE: s 15(3) restricts only objects of significant value, so other objects may be disposed of under the general power (s 7);
-- and since s 15(5) overrides a prohibiting trust only for a s 15(4) disposal, the encoding treats such a trust as binding otherwise.
GIVEN `of significant national or historical value` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a duplicate` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `unsuitable for retention in the Board's opinion` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Minister approved beforehand` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `useless through damage, deterioration or infestation` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a trust or condition prohibits disposal` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the means` IS A `Means of disposal`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may dispose of the object` IF
    IF `useless through damage, deterioration or infestation` THEN TRUE
    ELSE IF `a trust or condition prohibits disposal` THEN FALSE
         ELSE IF `of significant national or historical value`
              THEN (`a duplicate` OR `unsuitable for retention in the Board's opinion`)
                   AND `the Minister approved beforehand`
                   AND (NOT (`the means` EQUALS destruction))
              ELSE TRUE

-- s 16(3): where an object vested in the Board "subject to a condition", the power to lend "is exercisable in a manner inconsistent
-- with the condition if either (a) 25 years have elapsed since the date on which the property became vested in the Board; or (b) the
-- person who first imposed the condition or his or her personal representatives have consented in writing".
GIVEN `the loan is inconsistent with a condition` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `years since the object vested` IS A NUMBER,
      `the imposer or personal representatives consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may lend the object` IF
        (NOT `the loan is inconsistent with a condition`)
    OR  `years since the object vested` AT LEAST 25
    OR  `the imposer or personal representatives consented in writing`

§§ `4, 5 and the Schedule -- the Board as a body`

-- s 4(2): a sealed document "must be signed by (a) any 2 members of the Board generally or specially authorised by the Board for the
-- purpose; or (b) one member ... so authorised ... and the chief executive officer".
GIVEN `authorised members signing` IS A NUMBER, `the chief executive officer signed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sealed document is properly signed` IF
        `authorised members signing` AT LEAST 2
    OR  (`authorised members signing` AT LEAST 1 AND `the chief executive officer signed`)

-- s 5(1): a Chairperson, a Deputy Chairperson and "not less than 10 and not more than 25 other members".
GIVEN `other members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board has a lawful number of other members` IF
    `other members` AT LEAST 10 AND `other members` AT MOST 25

-- Schedule para 9: no person may be appointed or continue as a member if he or she "(a) has a mental disorder and is incapable of
-- managing himself or herself or his or her affairs; (b) is an undischarged bankrupt or has made any arrangement or composition with
-- his or her creditors; or (c) is convicted of an offence involving dishonesty, fraud or moral turpitude and has not received a free
-- pardon". Para 7: office is vacated if the member "(a) becomes in any manner disqualified" or "(b) has been absent, without leave of
-- the Board, from 3 consecutive meetings".
GIVEN `incapable through mental disorder` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `an undischarged bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `made an arrangement with creditors` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `convicted of an offence of dishonesty, fraud or moral turpitude` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `received a free pardon` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is disqualified from membership` IF
        `incapable through mental disorder`
    OR  `an undischarged bankrupt`
    OR  `made an arrangement with creditors`
    OR  (`convicted of an offence of dishonesty, fraud or moral turpitude` AND (NOT `received a free pardon`))

GIVEN `disqualified` IS A BOOLEAN, `consecutive meetings missed without leave` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member's office is vacated` IF
    `disqualified` OR `consecutive meetings missed without leave` AT LEAST 3

-- Schedule para 11(2): "The quorum for a meeting of the Board is one-half of the total number of members." (3): decisions "by a simple
-- majority of the votes of the members present and voting; and in the case of an equality of votes, the Chairperson or in his or her
-- absence the Deputy Chairperson or the member presiding has a casting vote".
GIVEN `members present` IS A NUMBER, `total members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the meeting is quorate` IF
    `members present` TIMES 2 AT LEAST `total members`

GIVEN `votes for` IS A NUMBER, `votes against` IS A NUMBER, `the presiding member's casting vote is for` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the motion is carried` IF
        `votes for` GREATER THAN `votes against`
    OR  (`votes for` EQUALS `votes against` AND `the presiding member's casting vote is for`)
